<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. upland cotton major sales activity in the week ended Sept 19 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in 1,000 running bales:</p>
<p> Net Sales:   1996/97	   1997/98</p>
<p>  Japan	 50,000		Nil</p>
<p>  S Korea     30,400</p>
<p>  China	 13,800</p>
<p>  Indonesia   13,400</p>
<p>  Mexico	 7,600</p>
<p>Net sales of 123,500 running bales fell 19 percent from the previous week and were 63 percent above the four-week average.</p>
<p>Weekly exports of 33,300 running bales were 39 percent down from the previous week.</p>
<p>Asian destinations accounted for 61 percent of the weeks shipments, and the Western Hemisphere 38 percent.</p>
</text>
